15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing mean PCL-5 scores for EMDR, CBT, and Control groups at three time points. Both EMDR and CBT groups show notable score reductions, with EMDR declining most steeply, while Control remains stable.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart comparing pre-post effect sizes \(Cohen's d\) for EMDR and CBT across four measures: PTSD, Depression, Anxiety, and Emotion Regulation. EMDR shows higher effect sizes for PTSD and Depression, while CBT shows higher effect sizes for Emotion Regulation and slightly higher for Anxiety. Legend identifies EMDR in yellow and CBT in orange. Data source is not specified.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart comparing change scores for four outcomes\204PTSD, depression, anxiety, and emotion regulation\204among EMDR, CBT, and control groups. EMDR and CBT groups show greater improvement than control across outcomes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
